chip-dt-overlays (0.8) trixie; urgency=high

  * Rename the maintained mainline overlays to the x-chip-* convention:
    x-chip-pocketchip, x-chip-dip-hdmi, x-chip-dip-vga, and the experimental
    i2c-gpio (bitbang) HDMI variant x-chip-dip-hdmi-gpio. The bootscript DIP
    auto-select (x-chip-os) references these by PID.
  * Drop the superseded keyboard-only overlay (folded into x-chip-pocketchip).
  * Move the original NextThing 4.4-era overlays and their EEPROM-PID symlinks
    to firmware/deprecated/ (not built or shipped; kept for historical
    reference only -- see firmware/deprecated/README.md).
  * Add full PocketCHIP overlay (chip-pocketchip): Olimex RGB panel + PWM
    backlight + resistive touch + TCA8418 keyboard, ported from the
    pocketchip-debian-builder mainline overlay (real-hardware validated).
  * HDMI/VGA overlays: disable tve0 + the composite tcon0_out endpoint so
    tcon0 drives only the RGB channel into the bridge/DAC.

 -- Ben Young <computermouth@proton.me>  Fri, 12 Jun 2026 18:30:00 -0500

